title: Files Jeff is editing during a run
pid: 35521121-0a21-40d4-b725-dacc5d2003de
body: |2-
  Jeff reads and annotates the plan and the review while a run is
  on, so the plan file, the review and the glossary are often dirty
  with his edits when an agent starts. The brief names them, and the
  agent commits only its own hunks of such a file: it writes a copy
  of HEAD's version plus its own edits and puts that copy in the
  index ('git update-index' with the blob, or 'git apply --cached'
  with a patch against HEAD), leaving Jeff's hunks unstaged in the
  working tree. This worked for every slice of plan 4. If a hunk
  cannot be separated, the agent leaves that edit out and says so.
